{"version_id": 64, "article_id": 7, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Ex-German spy chief arrested on suspicion of treason", "title_zh": "德国前情报局长因涉嫌叛国被捕", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c58jzyer1kr0o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Helmut_Schmidt%2C_former_German_Chancellor.jpg", "credit": "No machine-readable author provided. Axel Sperl assumed (based on copyright clai · cc0 1.0 · via wikimedia"}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 265, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "A former head of Germany's intelligence service has been arrested. Prosecutors say he passed classified information to foreign powers, and a former colleague is also accused.", "lead_zh": "德国情报机构前负责人已被逮捕。检方称他向外国势力传递了机密信息，一名前同事也受到指控。", "preview": "August Hanning, who led Germany's Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005, has been arrested on suspicion of espionage and trea", "preview_zh": "曾于1998年至2005年领导德国联邦情报局（BND）的奥古斯特·汉宁因涉嫌间谍活动和叛国被捕。检方称，他利用机密情报为一家外国情报机构撰写分析报告，并与另一家机构保持联系。检方未透露涉及哪些国家。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 54, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@a79b424/content/audio/7/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 109.675, "size_bytes": 661824, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 294, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@a79b424/content/data/versions/64.json", "paragraphs": ["August Hanning, who led Germany's Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005, has been arrested on suspicion of espionage and treason. Prosecutors claim he used classified intelligence to prepare an analysis for one foreign service and stayed in contact with another. They have not said which countries were involved.", "Police also arrested a former BND employee called Manfred D. He is accused of giving Hanning about 2,000 classified documents in exchange for money. Manfred D was Hanning's bureau chief and remained in the BND until this year, later serving as chief of staff for Hanning's successors.", "According to prosecutors, Manfred D used his position to access highly confidential material, which he then passed to Hanning for payment. On one occasion, Hanning allegedly used secret intelligence to draft an analysis for an officer of a foreign service, though it is unclear whether the material reached its intended recipient.", "Hanning is also accused of having close contact with a representative of another foreign intelligence service, to whom he passed political information over several years. Local media reported that Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde, while Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria. Hanning is due in court on Wednesday, and Manfred D on Tuesday.", "The case reportedly came to light during a separate investigation involving Christina Block, a German steakhouse heiress accused of organising the kidnapping of her two youngest children in 2023. Police reportedly found an electronic storage device containing sensitive BND documents. This is not the first such scandal: in 2023, a senior intelligence officer was charged with passing state secrets to Russia."], "paragraphs_zh": ["曾于1998年至2005年领导德国联邦情报局（BND）的奥古斯特·汉宁因涉嫌间谍活动和叛国被捕。检方称，他利用机密情报为一家外国情报机构撰写分析报告，并与另一家机构保持联系。检方未透露涉及哪些国家。", "警方还逮捕了一名名为曼弗雷德·D的前BND雇员。他被指控以金钱为交换，向汉宁提供了约2000份机密文件。曼弗雷德·D曾是汉宁的办公室主任，今年之前一直在BND任职，后来还担任过汉宁继任者的幕僚长。", "检方称，曼弗雷德·D利用职务之便获取了高度机密的材料，然后交给汉宁以换取报酬。有一次，汉宁涉嫌利用秘密情报为一家外国情报机构的官员起草分析报告，但尚不清楚材料是否送达了预定接收人。", "汉宁还被指控与另一家外国情报机构的代表保持密切联系，并在数年间向其传递政治信息。当地媒体报道称，汉宁在明斯特附近的诺德瓦尔德家中被捕，而曼弗雷德·D在巴伐利亚被捕。汉宁将于周三出庭，曼弗雷德·D将于周二出庭。", "据报道，此案是在另一起调查中曝光的，该调查涉及德国牛排馆女继承人克里斯蒂娜·布洛克，她被指控在2023年策划绑架自己两个最小的孩子。警方据称发现了一个存有敏感BND文件的电子存储设备。这并非首例此类丑闻：2023年，一名高级情报官员因涉嫌向俄罗斯传递国家机密而被起诉。"], "body": "August Hanning, who led Germany's Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005, has been arrested on suspicion of espionage and treason. Prosecutors claim he used classified intelligence to prepare an analysis for one foreign service and stayed in contact with another. They have not said which countries were involved.\n\nPolice also arrested a former BND employee called Manfred D. He is accused of giving Hanning about 2,000 classified documents in exchange for money. Manfred D was Hanning's bureau chief and remained in the BND until this year, later serving as chief of staff for Hanning's successors.\n\nAccording to prosecutors, Manfred D used his position to access highly confidential material, which he then passed to Hanning for payment. On one occasion, Hanning allegedly used secret intelligence to draft an analysis for an officer of a foreign service, though it is unclear whether the material reached its intended recipient.\n\nHanning is also accused of having close contact with a representative of another foreign intelligence service, to whom he passed political information over several years. Local media reported that Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde, while Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria. Hanning is due in court on Wednesday, and Manfred D on Tuesday.\n\nThe case reportedly came to light during a separate investigation involving Christina Block, a German steakhouse heiress accused of organising the kidnapping of her two youngest children in 2023. Police reportedly found an electronic storage device containing sensitive BND documents. This is not the first such scandal: in 2023, a senior intelligence officer was charged with passing state secrets to Russia.", "body_zh": "曾于1998年至2005年领导德国联邦情报局（BND）的奥古斯特·汉宁因涉嫌间谍活动和叛国被捕。检方称，他利用机密情报为一家外国情报机构撰写分析报告，并与另一家机构保持联系。检方未透露涉及哪些国家。\n\n警方还逮捕了一名名为曼弗雷德·D的前BND雇员。他被指控以金钱为交换，向汉宁提供了约2000份机密文件。曼弗雷德·D曾是汉宁的办公室主任，今年之前一直在BND任职，后来还担任过汉宁继任者的幕僚长。\n\n检方称，曼弗雷德·D利用职务之便获取了高度机密的材料，然后交给汉宁以换取报酬。有一次，汉宁涉嫌利用秘密情报为一家外国情报机构的官员起草分析报告，但尚不清楚材料是否送达了预定接收人。\n\n汉宁还被指控与另一家外国情报机构的代表保持密切联系，并在数年间向其传递政治信息。当地媒体报道称，汉宁在明斯特附近的诺德瓦尔德家中被捕，而曼弗雷德·D在巴伐利亚被捕。汉宁将于周三出庭，曼弗雷德·D将于周二出庭。\n\n据报道，此案是在另一起调查中曝光的，该调查涉及德国牛排馆女继承人克里斯蒂娜·布洛克，她被指控在2023年策划绑架自己两个最小的孩子。警方据称发现了一个存有敏感BND文件的电子存储设备。这并非首例此类丑闻：2023年，一名高级情报官员因涉嫌向俄罗斯传递国家机密而被起诉。", "text": "August Hanning, who led Germany's Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005, has been arrested on suspicion of espionage and treason. Prosecutors claim he used classified intelligence to prepare an analysis for one foreign service and stayed in contact with another. They have not said which countries were involved. Police also arrested a former BND employee called Manfred D. He is accused of giving Hanning about 2,000 classified documents in exchange for money. Manfred D was Hanning's bureau chief and remained in the BND until this year, later serving as chief of staff for Hanning's successors. According to prosecutors, Manfred D used his position to access highly confidential material, which he then passed to Hanning for payment. On one occasion, Hanning allegedly used secret intelligence to draft an analysis for an officer of a foreign service, though it is unclear whether the material reached its intended recipient. Hanning is also accused of having close contact with a representative of another foreign intelligence service, to whom he passed political information over several years. Local media reported that Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde, while Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria. Hanning is due in court on Wednesday, and Manfred D on Tuesday. The case reportedly came to light during a separate investigation involving Christina Block, a German steakhouse heiress accused of organising the kidnapping of her two youngest children in 2023. Police reportedly found an electronic storage device containing sensitive BND documents. This is not the first such scandal: in 2023, a senior intelligence officer was charged with passing state secrets to Russia.", "vocab": [{"word": "espionage", "pos": "noun", "zh": "间谍活动", "note": "常与 treason 连用，指为外国收集情报的行为"}, {"word": "treason", "pos": "noun", "zh": "叛国罪", "note": "法律用语，指危害国家的严重罪行"}, {"word": "classified", "pos": "adj", "zh": "机密的", "note": "指政府或军方限制公开的信息"}, {"word": "prosecutor", "pos": "noun", "zh": "检察官", "note": "负责提起刑事诉讼的官员"}, {"word": "allege", "pos": "verb", "zh": "指控；声称", "note": "常用于被动语态，表示未经证实的说法"}, {"word": "suspicion", "pos": "noun", "zh": "怀疑；嫌疑", "note": "常见搭配 on suspicion of"}, {"word": "confidential", "pos": "adj", "zh": "机密的", "note": "比 classified 语气稍弱，指不宜公开的"}, {"word": "bureau chief", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "办公室主任；分社社长", "note": "指机构中负责一个部门的领导"}, {"word": "in exchange for", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "作为交换", "note": "常接金钱或利益，表示交换条件"}, {"word": "recipient", "pos": "noun", "zh": "接收者", "note": "指收到某物的人或机构"}, {"word": "scandal", "pos": "noun", "zh": "丑闻", "note": "指引起公众震惊的不当行为"}, {"word": "custody dispute", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "监护权纠纷", "note": "指父母之间关于孩子抚养权的法律争议"}], "title_original": "Former German spy chief arrested for espionage and treason", "summary_original": "August Hanning is accused of obtaining classified information for a foreign power.", "body_original": "Former German spy chief arrested for espionage and treason\nBy\nOlivia Ireland\nPublished\n6 hours ago\nFormer German spy chief August Hanning has been arrested on suspicion of espionage, treason and obtaining classified information for a foreign power, the German Federal Prosecutor's Office says.\nHanning headed the Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005 and has since been working as a private consultant.\nProsecutors allege that he used classified intelligence to \"draft an analysis\" for one foreign intelligence service and maintained contact with another foreign spying service. Investigators have not disclosed which foreign powers were involved.\nPolice also arrested former BND employee Manfred D, accusing him of passing Hanning about 2,000 classified documents for money.\nManfred D, who was Hanning's bureau chief and remained in the BND until this year, is charged with aiding and abetting attempted treason and treasonous espionage.\nLocal media reported Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde near Münster while Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria. Hanning is due in court on Wednesday and Manfred D will appear on Tuesday.\nProsecutors say Manfred D, who also served as the chief of staff for Hanning's successors between 2012 and 2026, used his role to gain access to highly confidential information which he then passed on to Hanning \"in exchange for remuneration\".\n\"The current findings suggest that, over the years, Manfred D provided Hanning with approximately 2,000 documents, many of which contained classified information to be used exclusively by the Federal Intelligence Service for internal purposes,\" the statement says.\n\"On one occasion, Hanning used classified intelligence ... to draft an analysis for an officer of a foreign intelligence service,\" prosecutors said, noting it was not clear if \"the material reached the intended recipient\".\nHanning is also accused of being \"in close contact with a representative of another foreign intelligence service, to whom he passed on political information, partially based on material provided by Manfred D, for several years\".\nLocal media say Hanning's alleged possession of intelligence documents came to light during a separate case relating to German steakhouse heiress Christina Block.\nHamburg public prosecutor's office accused Block of orchestrating the kidnapping of her two youngest children in 2023 due to a custody dispute. Investigators allege Hanning was involved in an earlier attempted kidnapping of the children, which he denies.\nState criminal police officers reportedly discovered an electronic data storage device containing sensitive information including recent BND documents.\nIt is not the first time the BND has faced similar controversy. A high-ranking German intelligence officer was\ncharged with treason in 2023\nfor allegedly passing state secrets to Russia.\nProsecutors alleged Carsten L shared intelligence about the war in Ukraine and the Wagner mercenary group and received roughly €400,000 ($450,000; £340,000). His trial is ongoing.\nRelated topics\nGermany\nCorruption\nSpying\nMore on this story\nAlmost 60,000 far-right extremists in Germany, intelligence agency says\nPublished\n30 June\nGermany investigates Russia links to weapons cache discovered in woods, reports say\nPublished\n21 August", "fetched_at": "2026-10-06T16:57:31.470498+00:00", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "August", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.512, "sm": 100, "em": 512, "cs": 0, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Hanning", "s": 0.525, "e": 0.913, "sm": 525, "em": 912, "cs": 7, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": ",", "s": 0.913, "e": 1.113, "sm": 912, "em": 1112, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "who", "s": 1.113, "e": 1.213, "sm": 1112, "em": 1212, "cs": 16, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "led", "s": 1.225, "e": 1.475, "sm": 1225, "em": 1475, "cs": 20, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "Germany's", "s": 1.488, "e": 2.013, "sm": 1487, "em": 2012, "cs": 24, "ce": 33, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "Federal", "s": 2.025, "e": 2.362, "sm": 2025, "em": 2362, "cs": 34, "ce": 41, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "Intelligence", "s": 2.375, "e": 3.0, "sm": 2375, "em": 3000, "cs": 42, "ce": 54, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "Service", "s": 3.013, "e": 3.463, "sm": 3012, "em": 3462, "cs": 55, "ce": 62, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "(", "s": 3.463, "e": 3.65, "sm": 3462, "em": 3650, "cs": 63, "ce": 64, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "BND", "s": 3.65, "e": 4.325, "sm": 3650, "em": 4325, "cs": 64, "ce": 67, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": ")", "s": 4.325, "e": 4.588, "sm": 4325, "em": 4587, "cs": 67, "ce": 68, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "from", "s": 4.588, "e": 5.248, "sm": 4587, "em": 5248, "cs": 69, "ce": 73, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "1998", "s": 5.248, "e": 5.909, "sm": 5248, "em": 5908, "cs": 74, "ce": 78, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "to", "s": 5.909, "e": 6.239, "sm": 5908, "em": 6239, "cs": 79, "ce": 81, "si": 0}, {"i": 15, "w": "2005", "s": 6.23